SRC/lotto -- lotto, as built for OS-9/68000===========================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.games carried it.  getopt.c isunchanged.  lotto.c differs in two places:  - its usage text was one string continued over 16 lines, and Microware's    cpp joins continued lines into one before anything else, past its    513-character line.  The same text is kept in pieces and joined with    strcat() at start-up, and printf() is given it exactly as before.  - at end of input its yes-or-no question returned `no', and `Do you    believe?' is asked until the answer is yes -- so `lotto < /nil' never    ended.  Under #ifdef OSK end of input now exits.